{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c3eb","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0aa4d-35aa-7773-97f7-293f4760a2d6"},"sequence":80,"recorded_at":1780531400000155,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"a1715be3-1f15-4a95-87f8-c19d8786aea9","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"a1715be3-1f15-4a95-87f8-c19d8786aea9","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"a1715be3-1f15-4a95-87f8-c19d8786aea9"},"call_id":"call_01a0aa4d674676d5b65f5df35bc3d576","text":"Read text file `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/resources/TASK-260830-21gygk/TASK-260830-21gygk_rework-rev9.md`.\n1|Rework the full assigned name-query candidate of TASK-260830-21gygk after the CR9 independent changes-requested verdict by RUN-260916-968194 (Astra low). Read TASK-260830-21gygk_review-verdict-rev9.md and materialize TASK-260830-21gygk_review-evidence-rev9.tar.gz through resource get; it contains TestReview9ForkLocalProfile, TestReview9ResumeReferencedCheckpoint, the mutation-classification.md/json and raw logs. Candidate tree 6eb65f537f4ebffe6e6044f5b64ffc1b89d4487e, base 8cf4aaaa190e6a11dff2661aa6806ce476128653, managed Story worktree .temp/STORY-260830-3tq4ns/worktree on branch task-board/story/STORY-260830-3tq4ns with checkpoint 83640d19 (two checkpointed predecessors). Continue from the uncommitted CR9 candidate in that worktree; preserve checkpointed predecessors and all foreign changes; no manual commits, no direct .task-board editing, no self-acceptance. Superseded briefs (rework-rev8 and earlier) remain scope context only; this brief governs.\n2|\n3|This is the third consecutive verdict in the same family (CR7 heads, CR8 profile source, CR9 fork/resume): each fix closed the witnessed arm and left the next relation of the same pinned sentence unowned. Do not fix P1-A and P1-B as two more arms. First build the instrument that closes the class: a relation census derived from the pinned normative sentences — SPEC 5.2 \"The profile and profile-source pair in every launch, resume, and fork event MUST equal the Section 2.4 effective profile at the referenced checkpoint or, for the first launch, the Session Record and null; a non-null source MUST name the newest authoritative profile.changed event in that event-head closure; for fork.created the effective new-session authority is its newly persisted Session Record so profile_source_event_id is null; source_profile_event_id never participates\", plus the 2.4 effective-profile derivation and the 5.4 closure rules (no later local-only event is authority for an earlier checkpoint). The census is a table, one row per (event kind × relationship): provider.launched first launch, provider.launched later launch, task_board.launched first/later, session.resumed, fork.created; for each row the authority input (Session Record; effective profile at the REFERENCED checkpoint's own event-head closure — resolved through the event's checkpoint_id and the admitted Checkpoint Record, never the position in the outer walk), the production owner arm, the positive control, the negatives (missing/read-failed/contradictory/non-newest/later-local-only/losing-lease/wrong-session reference), and the narrowing plant. Every row must be either driven or declared a caller bound with the owning clause named; an undriven row is a finding, not a bound. Attach the census as TASK-260830-21gygk_relation-census-rev10.md and make it the C6 section of the conformance matrix.\n4|\n5|Then implement against the census in the shared owner (checkCheckpointProfileAuthority / checkClosureProfilePairs / checkProfilePairSource in internal/sessquery/lease.go): P1-A add the fork.created arm comparing the event pair to the NEW Session Record's creation profile with a null source while holding cross-session source_profile_event_id provenance as the explicit caller bound; P1-B derive the session.resumed expectation from the closure of its referenced checkpoint (supply the checkpoint-record inputs the owner needs; distinguish missing, read-failed and contradictory referenced authority with the right refusal class) and apply the same referenced-checkpoint derivation to later launches where 5.2 requires it. Port both reviewer probes RED first on the current source, keep their positive controls, then add winner/necessary-ancestor, direct/task_board, old-plan substitution and fresh-plan Revalidate variants through BuildPlan, Revalidate, AuthoritativeStatus and AuthoritativeList, with historical/branching/lagging controls preserved. Every new arm gets a qualifying narrowing plant whose kill is a behavioral admission failure, not a class-label failure.\n6|\n7|P2: correct the mutation accounting everywhere it is claimed (outcome, TRACEABILITY.md, LOGBOOK.md): the manifests hold 56 unique N/B plants, 39 semantic-admission and 17 label/class/output-precision, not 59 narrowing kills; N-checkpoint-heads is a class/order precision kill; report the three classifier controls (harmless SURVIVED applied, NOT_APPLIED, COMPILE_OR_HARNESS_FAILURE) separately and never in the numerator. Rerun the shipped instrument on the exact final source, keep per-plant raw logs in the evidence bundle, and take every exit from subprocess return codes, never from a pipeline tail.\n8|\n9|Retain closed findings: CR7 missing/later checkpoint heads and old-plan substitution; CR8 missing-source refusals and real profile changes; direct/task_board persistence variants; necessary ancestry/creator; canonical lease identity; lagging copies; parked required source; the seven capabilities; predecessor/reducer/enums/creation crashes. Preserve the accepted CLI/publication/storage/transport/effects boundary and the 8-row AC denominator (0 of 8 CLI rows, stated bound); correct partial/failing rows only with real evidence. Read the Curator-managed go-testing-tools skill first; all CI local; run the affected packages while iterating and the full configured validation before the normal producer handoff. Attach TASK-260830-21gygk_results-rev10.md, TASK-260830-21gygk_conformance-matrix-rev10.md, TASK-260830-21gygk_relation-census-rev10.md and TASK-260830-21gygk_producer-evidence-rev10.tar.gz, then hand off through the normal task-board CR lifecycle and exit promptly. Canonical CLI /Users/iv/.curator/global/bin/task-board. Model: muse muse-spark max. The independent reviewer will be codex gpt-6-astra low.","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
