{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c7f7","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0aa4d-35aa-7773-97f7-293f4760a2d6"},"sequence":598,"recorded_at":1780531400001191,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"a1715be3-1f15-4a95-87f8-c19d8786aea9","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"a1715be3-1f15-4a95-87f8-c19d8786aea9","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"a1715be3-1f15-4a95-87f8-c19d8786aea9"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0aa4e-946b-7260-b272-6ae7938ffb5f"},"task_id":"01a0aa4e-946b-7260-b272-6ae7938ffb5f","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0aa4e-946b-7260-b272-6ae7938ffb5f","chunk":"Read text file `internal/specdoc/SPEC.md`.\n(1794 line(s) above)\n1795|For <code>takeover.force_confirmed</code>, <code>accepted_risks</code> MUST be\n1796|exactly <code>[\"divergent_history\",\"split_brain\",\"stale_process\"]</code> in\n1797|bytewise order. For <code>task_board.launched</code> and\n1798|<code>task_board.adopted</code>, goal ID and revision MUST\n1799|either both be null or both be non-null, and a non-null revision is greater\n1800|than zero. A <code>task_board.launched</code> event MUST repeat the winning\n1801|creation lease and the Session Record's provider/launch mode; a mismatch is\n1802|<code>integrity_failure</code>. Audit event issuance and retention are specified\n1803|in Sections 10.7 and 18.4. A <code>tombstone.resolved</code> resurrection\n1804|requires a non-null resulting entry digest; every other resolution requires\n1805|null.\n1806|\n1807|The profile and profile-source pair in every launch, resume, and fork event\n1808|MUST equal the Section 2.4 effective profile at the referenced checkpoint or,\n1809|for the first launch, the Session Record and null. A non-null source MUST name\n1810|the newest authoritative <code>profile.changed</code> event in that event-head\n1811|closure. Equal provider mapping strings do not permit changing either value.\n1812|For <code>fork.created</code>, the effective new-session authority is its newly\n1813|persisted Session Record, so <code>profile_source_event_id</code> is null.\n1814|<code>source_profile_event_id</code> separately equals the nullable source-\n1815|checkpoint profile event and never participates in new-session derivation.\n1816|\n1817|A <code>session.stopped</code> payload is <code>checkpointed</code> exactly when\n1818|<code>checkpoint_id</code> is non-null and <code>resumable = true</code>.\n1819|<code>bootstrap_abort</code> requires a null checkpoint, false resumable and\n1820|graceful values, and a preceding or equal-operation\n1821|<code>session.bootstrap_aborted</code> event; its derived lifecycle is\n1822|<code>failed</code>, never <code>stopped</code>. A bootstrap-aborted event\n1823|requires both closure booleans true. Its identity fields are both null before\n1824|identity, and after identity exactly the field belonging to the Session Record\n1825|kind is non-null. An ambiguous live process or open store cannot be represented\n1826|as a successful abort and remains <code>failed</code> with recovery diagnostics.\n1827|\n1828|An unknown event type MUST be retained as an immutable object but MUST NOT\n1829|change derived session state under major version 1.\n1830|\n1831|Normative example:\n1832|\n1833|~~~json\n1834|{\n1835|  \"schema\": \"urn:ax:schema:session-event\",\n1836|  \"schema_version\": \"1.0.0\",\n1837|  \"event_id\": \"sha256:46d2745fe7dfce856027be36e34f1cc6a56ffc846063dc4aa6aabf3f5a85bacb\",\n1838|  \"subject_id\": \"0198f4c8-3e70-7a11-8a2b-1234567890ab\",\n1839|  \"session_id\": \"0198f4c8-3e70-7a11-8a2b-1234567890ab\",\n1840|  \"event_type\": \"session.stopped\",\n1841|  \"created_by_host_id\": \"0198f4c8-4a10-7b22-8b3c-1234567890ab\",\n1842|  \"lease_epoch\": 4,\n1843|  \"lease_id\": \"aaaaaaaa-bbbb-4ccc-8ddd-eeeeeeeeeeee\",\n1844|  \"lease_sequence\": 12,\n1845|  \"predecessors\": [\n1846|    \"sha256:7777777777777777777777777777777777777777777777777777777777777777\"\n1847|  ],\n1848|  \"created_at\": \"2026-08-19T04:08:00.000Z\",\n1849|  \"payload\": {\n1850|    \"graceful\": true,\n1851|    \"checkpoint_id\": \"sha256:e051996f51f13ace4f5cdebe1e30fd26fd5fe104cfd6e6a7f9f1206ba3819656\",\n1852|    \"resumable\": true,\n1853|    \"closure_kind\": \"checkpointed\",\n1854|    \"process_closed\": true,\n1855|    \"store_closed\": true\n1856|  },\n1857|  \"extensions\": {}\n1858|}\n1859|~~~\n1860|\n1861|#### Session Event 4.0.0 Terminal Instance events\n1862|\n1863|Session Event 4.0.0 retains the exact v3 top-level closed shape, digest rules,\n1864|lease ordering, predecessor rules, and complete v1-v3 event-type registry. It\n1865|changes exactly the payload definitions for <code>terminal.created</code> and\n1866|<code>session.resumed</code>; every other v1-v3 payload remains byte-for-byte\n1867|the definition selected by v3. The two v4 payloads are:\n1868|\n1869|| Event type | Exact payload members |\n1870|| --- | --- |\n1871|| <code>terminal.created</code> | <code>terminal_binding_id:digest</code>, <code>terminal_backend_id:terminal-backend-id</code>, <code>implementation_version:semver</code>, <code>protocol_version:semver</code>, <code>evidence_ids:sorted unique digest[1..256]</code> |\n1872|| <code>session.resumed</code> | <code>checkpoint_id:digest</code>, <code>execution_profile:standard&#124;yolo</code>, <code>profile_source_event_id:digest&#124;null</code>, <code>terminal_binding_id:digest</code>, <code>terminal_backend_id:terminal-backend-id</code>, <code>implementation_version:semver</code>, <code>protocol_version:semver</code>, <code>evidence_ids:sorted unique digest[1..256]</code> |\n1873|\n1874|The binding digest is an opaque audit reference to a host-local Terminal\n1875|Instance Binding; the binding object itself is not an event member and is not\n1876|replicated. The evidence IDs MUST resolve locally to validated, sanitized\n1877|Manifest, Probe, and applicable Capability Evidence objects bound to the event's\n1878|backend ID and versions. They MUST NOT resolve through the event to a native\n1879|reference, generation string, socket, pipe, endpoint, token, credential,\n1880|terminal output, PID/handle, or live-process fact.\n1881|\n1882|<code>terminal.created</code> records the backend selected for a new AX-\n1883|authorized activation. <code>session.resumed</code> records the backend used by\n1884|that owner resume. A valid takeover or owner resume MAY select a different\n1885|admitted destination backend and emits a new binding digest and v4 event; it\n1886|does not clone/fork the LogicalSession and never mutates an earlier event.\n1887|Attach or presentation-client activity emits neither event and cannot change\n1888|Owner/Replica, lease, or fencing state. A reader of v1-v3 may retain a v4 event\n1889|as inert immutable history but MUST NOT derive runtime state or write a lower-\n1890|version replacement.\n1891|\n1892|### 5.3 Lease Record and ownership\n1893|\n1894|The Lease Record schema is <code>urn:ax:schema:lease</code> version\n1895|<code>1.0.0</code>. Fields are:\n1896|\n1897|| Field | Type | Constraint |\n1898|| --- | --- | --- |\n1899|| <code>schema</code> | string | Exact Lease Record schema identifier |\n1900|| <code>schema_version</code> | semver | Exact <code>1.0.0</code> |\n1901|| <code>record_id</code> | digest | Canonical Lease Record digest |\n1902|| <code>subject_id</code> | UUIDv7 | Equal to <code>session_id</code> |\n1903|| <code>lease_id</code> | UUIDv4 | Cryptographically random unique fencing token |\n1904|| <code>session_id</code> | UUIDv7 | Lease scope |\n1905|| <code>epoch</code> | uint53 | Starts at 1; never decreases |\n1906|| <code>holder_host_id</code> | UUIDv7 | Proposed owner |\n1907|| <code>predecessor_lease_id</code> | UUIDv4 or null | Null only at epoch 1 |\n1908|| <code>reason</code> | enum | <code>create</code>, <code>graceful_takeover</code>, <code>force_takeover</code>, <code>recovery</code> |\n1909|| <code>checkpoint_id</code> | digest or null | Null only for epoch-1 <code>create</code>; otherwise the validated materialized handoff base |\n1910|| <code>issued_by_host_id</code> | UUIDv7 | Initiator |\n1911|| <code>created_by_host_id</code> | UUIDv7 | MUST equal <code>issued_by_host_id</code> |\n1912|| <code>created_at</code> | timestamp | Diagnostic only |\n1913|| <code>extensions</code> | object | Reverse-DNS extension keys only |\n1914|\n(more lines below)","final_result":true}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c7f9","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0aa4d-35aa-7773-97f7-293f4760a2d6"},"sequence":599,"recorded_at":1780531400001193,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"a1715be3-1f15-4a95-87f8-c19d8786aea9","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.completed","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"a1715be3-1f15-4a95-87f8-c19d8786aea9","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"a1715be3-1f15-4a95-87f8-c19d8786aea9"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0aa4e-946b-7260-b272-6ae7938ffb5f"},"task_id":"01a0aa4e-946b-7260-b272-6ae7938ffb5f","event":{"kind":"completed","task_id":"01a0aa4e-946b-7260-b272-6ae7938ffb5f"}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c7fb","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0aa4d-35aa-7773-97f7-293f4760a2d6"},"sequence":600,"recorded_at":1780531400001195,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"a1715be3-1f15-4a95-87f8-c19d8786aea9","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"a1715be3-1f15-4a95-87f8-c19d8786aea9","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"a1715be3-1f15-4a95-87f8-c19d8786aea9"},"call_id":"call_01a0aa4e8e6a74be9bcc424f37f61c10","text":"Read text file `internal/specdoc/SPEC.md`.\n(1794 line(s) above)\n1795|For <code>takeover.force_confirmed</code>, <code>accepted_risks</code> MUST be\n1796|exactly <code>[\"divergent_history\",\"split_brain\",\"stale_process\"]</code> in\n1797|bytewise order. For <code>task_board.launched</code> and\n1798|<code>task_board.adopted</code>, goal ID and revision MUST\n1799|either both be null or both be non-null, and a non-null revision is greater\n1800|than zero. A <code>task_board.launched</code> event MUST repeat the winning\n1801|creation lease and the Session Record's provider/launch mode; a mismatch is\n1802|<code>integrity_failure</code>. Audit event issuance and retention are specified\n1803|in Sections 10.7 and 18.4. A <code>tombstone.resolved</code> resurrection\n1804|requires a non-null resulting entry digest; every other resolution requires\n1805|null.\n1806|\n1807|The profile and profile-source pair in every launch, resume, and fork event\n1808|MUST equal the Section 2.4 effective profile at the referenced checkpoint or,\n1809|for the first launch, the Session Record and null. A non-null source MUST name\n1810|the newest authoritative <code>profile.changed</code> event in that event-head\n1811|closure. Equal provider mapping strings do not permit changing either value.\n1812|For <code>fork.created</code>, the effective new-session authority is its newly\n1813|persisted Session Record, so <code>profile_source_event_id</code> is null.\n1814|<code>source_profile_event_id</code> separately equals the nullable source-\n1815|checkpoint profile event and never participates in new-session derivation.\n1816|\n1817|A <code>session.stopped</code> payload is <code>checkpointed</code> exactly when\n1818|<code>checkpoint_id</code> is non-null and <code>resumable = true</code>.\n1819|<code>bootstrap_abort</code> requires a null checkpoint, false resumable and\n1820|graceful values, and a preceding or equal-operation\n1821|<code>session.bootstrap_aborted</code> event; its derived lifecycle is\n1822|<code>failed</code>, never <code>stopped</code>. A bootstrap-aborted event\n1823|requires both closure booleans true. Its identity fields are both null before\n1824|identity, and after identity exactly the field belonging to the Session Record\n1825|kind is non-null. An ambiguous live process or open store cannot be represented\n1826|as a successful abort and remains <code>failed</code> with recovery diagnostics.\n1827|\n1828|An unknown event type MUST be retained as an immutable object but MUST NOT\n1829|change derived session state under major version 1.\n1830|\n1831|Normative example:\n1832|\n1833|~~~json\n1834|{\n1835|  \"schema\": \"urn:ax:schema:session-event\",\n1836|  \"schema_version\": \"1.0.0\",\n1837|  \"event_id\": \"sha256:46d2745fe7dfce856027be36e34f1cc6a56ffc846063dc4aa6aabf3f5a85bacb\",\n1838|  \"subject_id\": \"0198f4c8-3e70-7a11-8a2b-1234567890ab\",\n1839|  \"session_id\": \"0198f4c8-3e70-7a11-8a2b-1234567890ab\",\n1840|  \"event_type\": \"session.stopped\",\n1841|  \"created_by_host_id\": \"0198f4c8-4a10-7b22-8b3c-1234567890ab\",\n1842|  \"lease_epoch\": 4,\n1843|  \"lease_id\": \"aaaaaaaa-bbbb-4ccc-8ddd-eeeeeeeeeeee\",\n1844|  \"lease_sequence\": 12,\n1845|  \"predecessors\": [\n1846|    \"sha256:7777777777777777777777777777777777777777777777777777777777777777\"\n1847|  ],\n1848|  \"created_at\": \"2026-08-19T04:08:00.000Z\",\n1849|  \"payload\": {\n1850|    \"graceful\": true,\n1851|    \"checkpoint_id\": \"sha256:e051996f51f13ace4f5cdebe1e30fd26fd5fe104cfd6e6a7f9f1206ba3819656\",\n1852|    \"resumable\": true,\n1853|    \"closure_kind\": \"checkpointed\",\n1854|    \"process_closed\": true,\n1855|    \"store_closed\": true\n1856|  },\n1857|  \"extensions\": {}\n1858|}\n1859|~~~\n1860|\n1861|#### Session Event 4.0.0 Terminal Instance events\n1862|\n1863|Session Event 4.0.0 retains the exact v3 top-level closed shape, digest rules,\n1864|lease ordering, predecessor rules, and complete v1-v3 event-type registry. It\n1865|changes exactly the payload definitions for <code>terminal.created</code> and\n1866|<code>session.resumed</code>; every other v1-v3 payload remains byte-for-byte\n1867|the definition selected by v3. The two v4 payloads are:\n1868|\n1869|| Event type | Exact payload members |\n1870|| --- | --- |\n1871|| <code>terminal.created</code> | <code>terminal_binding_id:digest</code>, <code>terminal_backend_id:terminal-backend-id</code>, <code>implementation_version:semver</code>, <code>protocol_version:semver</code>, <code>evidence_ids:sorted unique digest[1..256]</code> |\n1872|| <code>session.resumed</code> | <code>checkpoint_id:digest</code>, <code>execution_profile:standard&#124;yolo</code>, <code>profile_source_event_id:digest&#124;null</code>, <code>terminal_binding_id:digest</code>, <code>terminal_backend_id:terminal-backend-id</code>, <code>implementation_version:semver</code>, <code>protocol_version:semver</code>, <code>evidence_ids:sorted unique digest[1..256]</code> |\n1873|\n1874|The binding digest is an opaque audit reference to a host-local Terminal\n1875|Instance Binding; the binding object itself is not an event member and is not\n1876|replicated. The evidence IDs MUST resolve locally to validated, sanitized\n1877|Manifest, Probe, and applicable Capability Evidence objects bound to the event's\n1878|backend ID and versions. They MUST NOT resolve through the event to a native\n1879|reference, generation string, socket, pipe, endpoint, token, credential,\n1880|terminal output, PID/handle, or live-process fact.\n1881|\n1882|<code>terminal.created</code> records the backend selected for a new AX-\n1883|authorized activation. <code>session.resumed</code> records the backend used by\n1884|that owner resume. A valid takeover or owner resume MAY select a different\n1885|admitted destination backend and emits a new binding digest and v4 event; it\n1886|does not clone/fork the LogicalSession and never mutates an earlier event.\n1887|Attach or presentation-client activity emits neither event and cannot change\n1888|Owner/Replica, lease, or fencing state. A reader of v1-v3 may retain a v4 event\n1889|as inert immutable history but MUST NOT derive runtime state or write a lower-\n1890|version replacement.\n1891|\n1892|### 5.3 Lease Record and ownership\n1893|\n1894|The Lease Record schema is <code>urn:ax:schema:lease</code> version\n1895|<code>1.0.0</code>. Fields are:\n1896|\n1897|| Field | Type | Constraint |\n1898|| --- | --- | --- |\n1899|| <code>schema</code> | string | Exact Lease Record schema identifier |\n1900|| <code>schema_version</code> | semver | Exact <code>1.0.0</code> |\n1901|| <code>record_id</code> | digest | Canonical Lease Record digest |\n1902|| <code>subject_id</code> | UUIDv7 | Equal to <code>session_id</code> |\n1903|| <code>lease_id</code> | UUIDv4 | Cryptographically random unique fencing token |\n1904|| <code>session_id</code> | UUIDv7 | Lease scope |\n1905|| <code>epoch</code> | uint53 | Starts at 1; never decreases |\n1906|| <code>holder_host_id</code> | UUIDv7 | Proposed owner |\n1907|| <code>predecessor_lease_id</code> | UUIDv4 or null | Null only at epoch 1 |\n1908|| <code>reason</code> | enum | <code>create</code>, <code>graceful_takeover</code>, <code>force_takeover</code>, <code>recovery</code> |\n1909|| <code>checkpoint_id</code> | digest or null | Null only for epoch-1 <code>create</code>; otherwise the validated materialized handoff base |\n1910|| <code>issued_by_host_id</code> | UUIDv7 | Initiator |\n1911|| <code>created_by_host_id</code> | UUIDv7 | MUST equal <code>issued_by_host_id</code> |\n1912|| <code>created_at</code> | timestamp | Diagnostic only |\n1913|| <code>extensions</code> | object | Reverse-DNS extension keys only |\n1914|\n(more lines below)","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
