{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c821","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0aa4d-35aa-7773-97f7-293f4760a2d6"},"sequence":619,"recorded_at":1780531400001233,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"a1715be3-1f15-4a95-87f8-c19d8786aea9","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"a1715be3-1f15-4a95-87f8-c19d8786aea9","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"a1715be3-1f15-4a95-87f8-c19d8786aea9"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0aa4e-a013-7123-989d-2fe325688c0a"},"task_id":"01a0aa4e-a013-7123-989d-2fe325688c0a","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0aa4e-a013-7123-989d-2fe325688c0a","chunk":"Read text file `internal/specdoc/SPEC.md`.\n(2014 line(s) above)\n2015|meets its quiescence requirement. A force takeover MAY select the newest\n2016|validated checkpoint even when no new safe checkpoint can be created.\n2017|\n2018|<code>event_heads</code> identifies the authoritative event DAG immediately\n2019|before the checkpoint object. A later <code>checkpoint.created</code> event MAY\n2020|reference that checkpoint and those heads; the checkpoint MUST NOT reference\n2021|the announcing event because that would create a circular digest dependency.\n2022|The transitive event-head closure also fixes the Section 2.4 effective\n2023|execution profile and its nullable source event for this checkpoint. A missing,\n2024|losing-lease, or non-newest <code>profile.changed</code> reference is\n2025|<code>integrity_failure</code>; checkpoint consumers MUST NOT consult a later\n2026|local-only profile event or fall back to the creation profile.\n2027|\n2028|Normative negative fixtures are: <code>CP-N1</code>, with\n2029|<code>background_idle = false</code> and status <code>validated</code>;\n2030|<code>CP-N2</code>, with a direct Session Record and null provider manifest;\n2031|<code>CP-N3</code>, with both persistence IDs non-null; and\n2032|<code>CP-N4</code>, with an unknown <code>safe_boundary.pid</code> member. Each\n2033|MUST be rejected with <code>incompatible_schema</code> before publication.\n2034|\n2035|Normative example:\n2036|\n2037|~~~json\n2038|{\n2039|  \"schema\": \"urn:ax:schema:checkpoint\",\n2040|  \"schema_version\": \"1.0.0\",\n2041|  \"checkpoint_id\": \"sha256:e051996f51f13ace4f5cdebe1e30fd26fd5fe104cfd6e6a7f9f1206ba3819656\",\n2042|  \"subject_id\": \"0198f4c8-3e70-7a11-8a2b-1234567890ab\",\n2043|  \"session_id\": \"0198f4c8-3e70-7a11-8a2b-1234567890ab\",\n2044|  \"lease_epoch\": 4,\n2045|  \"lease_id\": \"aaaaaaaa-bbbb-4ccc-8ddd-eeeeeeeeeeee\",\n2046|  \"safe_boundary\": {\n2047|    \"provider_id\": \"codex\",\n2048|    \"provider_version\": \"0.147.0\",\n2049|    \"evidence\": \"accepted_test\",\n2050|    \"input_blocked\": true,\n2051|    \"foreground_idle\": true,\n2052|    \"background_idle\": true,\n2053|    \"open_processes\": 0,\n2054|    \"open_database_handles\": 0\n2055|  },\n2056|  \"event_heads\": [\n2057|    \"sha256:7777777777777777777777777777777777777777777777777777777777777777\"\n2058|  ],\n2059|  \"workspace_manifest_id\": \"sha256:a98ca90522b4de30e4aaaf9bf50529d09e15a817ffa67f94552fb313d1a1ad2e\",\n2060|  \"provider_manifest_id\": \"sha256:1e817955dcc529e282ab31f91c99561d03b3c5642282d2e0a0e05b0f60dd0f91\",\n2061|  \"task_board_bundle_id\": null,\n2062|  \"created_by_host_id\": \"0198f4c8-4a10-7b22-8b3c-1234567890ab\",\n2063|  \"created_at\": \"2026-08-19T04:09:30.000Z\",\n2064|  \"status\": \"validated\",\n2065|  \"extensions\": {}\n2066|}\n2067|~~~\n2068|\n2069|### 5.5 Provider Identity Record\n2070|\n2071|The Provider Identity Record schema is\n2072|<code>urn:ax:schema:provider-identity</code> version <code>1.0.0</code>. Its\n2073|top-level object is closed and contains exactly:\n2074|\n2075|| Field | Type | Constraint |\n2076|| --- | --- | --- |\n2077|| <code>schema</code> | string | Exact Provider Identity schema identifier |\n2078|| <code>schema_version</code> | semver | Exact <code>1.0.0</code> |\n2079|| <code>record_id</code> | digest | Canonical object digest |\n2080|| <code>subject_id</code> | UUIDv7 | Equal to <code>session_id</code> |\n2081|| <code>session_id</code> | UUIDv7 | Existing logical session |\n2082|| <code>provider_id</code> | provider-id | Must equal the Session Record provider |\n2083|| <code>provider_version</code> | string[1..128] | Exact probed version |\n2084|| <code>provider_version_range</code> | string[1..256] | Adapter compatibility range used for this identity |\n2085|| <code>native_session_id</code> | string[1..512] | Opaque provider handle; never interpreted by core |\n2086|| <code>identity_kind</code> | enum | <code>session_uuid</code>, <code>session_path_or_id</code>, <code>backend_conversation_uuid</code>, <code>task_board_managed</code>, or <code>provider_defined</code> |\n2087|| <code>logical_workspace_id</code> | UUIDv7 | Member of the Session Record workspace group |\n2088|| <code>backend_realm_fingerprint</code> | digest or null | Non-secret fingerprint; non-null when backend/account realm is a resume precondition |\n2089|| <code>opaque_identity</code> | map(provider-identity-key,string[1..1024])[0..32] | Explicit adapter data map defined below |\n2090|| <code>created_by_host_id</code> | UUIDv7 | Identifying owner host |\n2091|| <code>created_at</code> | timestamp | Diagnostic only |\n2092|| <code>extensions</code> | object | Reverse-DNS extension keys only |\n2093|\n2094|A provider-identity key matches <code>[a-z][a-z0-9_.-]{0,63}</code>. Map keys\n2095|are data rather than schema members; values are non-secret strings only. This\n2096|is the sole provider-defined identity-data surface in version 1.0.0. It MUST\n2097|NOT contain an absolute path, credential, environment value, PID, socket,\n2098|terminal ID, or mutable cache selector. Structured or binary provider data\n2099|belongs in a content-addressed provider manifest, not this map.\n2100|\n2101|An absolute workspace path MAY appear only as source observation metadata. It\n2102|MUST NOT be part of the cross-host identity. The destination adapter MUST\n2103|derive native path keys from the destination workspace mapping.\n2104|\n2105|Normative negative fixtures are: unknown <code>identity_kind</code>; absent\n2106|<code>opaque_identity</code>; a map value that is an object instead of a\n2107|string; an absolute source path in that map; or an Antigravity\n2108|<code>backend_conversation_uuid</code> with null realm fingerprint. Each MUST\n2109|fail schema or provider-identity validation. A backend fingerprint is optional\n2110|for the other kinds unless that provider's Section 8 contract requires it.\n2111|\n2112|Normative example:\n2113|\n2114|~~~json\n2115|{\n2116|  \"schema\": \"urn:ax:schema:provider-identity\",\n2117|  \"schema_version\": \"1.0.0\",\n2118|  \"record_id\": \"sha256:c879d766da67a8cfb3a3f6eae2234faa5d52d8df987496eae2218f40e5e220c2\",\n2119|  \"subject_id\": \"0198f4c8-3e70-7a11-8a2b-1234567890ab\",\n2120|  \"session_id\": \"0198f4c8-3e70-7a11-8a2b-1234567890ab\",\n2121|  \"provider_id\": \"antigravity\",\n2122|  \"provider_version\": \"1.1.14\",\n2123|  \"provider_version_range\": \">=1.1.14 <1.2.0\",\n2124|  \"native_session_id\": \"11111111-2222-4333-8444-555555555555\",\n2125|  \"identity_kind\": \"backend_conversation_uuid\",\n2126|  \"logical_workspace_id\": \"0198f4c8-6c30-7d44-8d5e-1234567890ab\",\n2127|  \"backend_realm_fingerprint\": \"sha256:aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaad\",\n2128|  \"opaque_identity\": {},\n2129|  \"created_by_host_id\": \"0198f4c8-4a10-7b22-8b3c-1234567890ab\",\n2130|  \"created_at\": \"2026-08-19T04:09:45.000Z\",\n2131|  \"extensions\": {}\n2132|}\n2133|~~~\n2134|\n2135|### 5.6 Workspace Group Record\n2136|\n2137|The Workspace Group Record schema is <code>urn:ax:schema:workspace-group</code>\n2138|version <code>1.0.0</code>. Its closed top-level shape contains exactly\n2139|<code>schema</code>, <code>schema_version</code>,\n2140|<code>record_id:digest</code>, <code>subject_id:UUIDv7</code>,\n2141|<code>workspace_group_id:UUIDv7</code>,\n2142|<code>display_name:string[1..128]</code>,\n2143|<code>members:WorkspaceMember[1..256]</code>,\n2144|<code>created_by_host_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>created_at:timestamp</code>, and\n(more lines below)","final_result":true}}}
