{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000ca37","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0aa4d-35aa-7773-97f7-293f4760a2d6"},"sequence":886,"recorded_at":1780531400001767,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"a1715be3-1f15-4a95-87f8-c19d8786aea9","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"a1715be3-1f15-4a95-87f8-c19d8786aea9","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"a1715be3-1f15-4a95-87f8-c19d8786aea9"},"call_id":"call_01a0aa4f5d00741fb421d465fad70495","text":"Read text file `internal/sessquery/query.go`.\n(99 line(s) above)\n100|// owners. They are consulted only by that layer: List and Status keep\n101|// the internal read model and refuse only the unrepresentable\n102|// record-only bootstrap.\n103|//\n104|// LeaseRecords carries the validated winning-lease authority for plan\n105|// construction and revalidation, from the lease owner. Each entry is\n106|// canonical JSON for one urn:ax:schema:lease Lease Record; the reader\n107|// validates the closed shape and canonical self identity through the\n108|// canonicaljson owner, selects the greatest (epoch, lease_id) winner\n109|// per session, and binds that record digest with its tuple and holder.\n110|// Absence for a session refuses observation_unavailable; malformed\n111|// bytes refuse invalid_config. Envelope observations never substitute\n112|// for these records.\n113|//\n114|// CheckpointRecords carries the validated checkpoint authority the\n115|// winning-lease succession gate requires, from the checkpoint owner.\n116|// Each entry is canonical JSON for one urn:ax:schema:checkpoint\n117|// Checkpoint Record; the reader validates the closed shape and\n118|// canonical self identity through the sessrepo owner. Every successor\n119|// winner must reference an admitted record for its session and\n120|// predecessor lease, carrying the persistence variant the referenced\n121|// Session Record kind selects; an unresolvable, misbound, or\n122|// wrong-variant reference refuses observation_unavailable, and\n123|// malformed bytes refuse invalid_config.\n124|type Reader struct {\n125|\tLocal              *sessrepo.Repository\n126|\tLocalHostID        string\n127|\tAllowlistedPeerIDs []string\n128|\tPeers              []PeerIndex\n129|\tAliases            map[string]string\n130|\tHostMetadata       map[string]HostMetadata\n131|\tObservations       map[string]SessionObservations\n132|\tLeaseRecords       [][]byte\n133|\tCheckpointRecords  [][]byte\n134|}\n135|\n136|// Summary contains only facts derived from verified session records and events.\n137|// It is an internal read model, not the closed Section 14.2 CLI SessionSummary.\n138|// Unknown owner/lease and parked diagnostics remain explicit in Projection.\n139|// Host display names, checkpoint timestamps/age, workspace state, capabilities,\n140|// process liveness and sync timestamps require their respective observation\n141|// owners and are deliberately not inferred from a record or a successful read.\n142|type Summary struct {\n143|\tProjection sessstate.Projection\n144|}\n145|\n146|// List reads local summaries in bytewise session-ID order. Parked sessions stay\n147|// visible with their blocking reason and retry; failure to enumerate the index\n148|// fails the read. No durable state is written, even for an interrupted create.\n149|// A complete read proving a record without any valid lease refuses the whole\n150|// list with selector_bootstrap_incomplete: the interrupted prefix is never\n151|// silently omitted and never returned as a public summary.\n152|func (reader *Reader) List() ([]Summary, error) {\n153|\tif reader == nil || reader.Local == nil {\n154|\t\treturn nil, fmt.Errorf(\"%w: local repository is required\", ErrUnavailable)\n155|\t}\n156|\trows, err := reader.read(reader.Local)\n157|\tif err != nil {\n158|\t\treturn nil, err\n159|\t}\n160|\tfor _, row := range rows {\n161|\t\tif err := checkSummaryRepresentable(row); err != nil {\n162|\t\t\treturn nil, err\n163|\t\t}\n164|\t}\n165|\treturn rows, nil\n166|}\n167|\n168|func (reader *Reader) read(repo *sessrepo.Repository) ([]Summary, error) {\n169|\trows, err := repo.ListSessions()\n170|\tif err != nil {\n171|\t\treturn nil, err\n172|\t}\n173|\tout := make([]Summary, 0, len(rows))\n174|\tprojector := sessstate.Projector{Repo: repo, LocalHostID: reader.LocalHostID}\n175|\tfor _, row := range rows {\n176|\t\tprojection, err := projector.Project(row.SessionID)\n177|\t\tif err != nil {\n178|\t\t\treturn nil, err\n179|\t\t}\n180|\t\tout = append(out, Summary{Projection: projection})\n181|\t}\n182|\tsort.Slice(out, func(i, j int) bool { return out[i].Projection.SessionID < out[j].Projection.SessionID })\n183|\treturn out, nil\n184|}\n185|\n186|// Status resolves any selector — bare, \"id:\", or source-qualified — through\n187|// the same path as Resolve, then projects from the selected repository. It\n188|// never treats a failed read as not found. Parked sessions can be inspected\n189|// by ID through InspectLocal, independently of live-name routing, so\n190|// operators retain access to the recovery diagnostics.\n191|func (reader *Reader) Status(selector string) (Summary, error) {\n192|\tselected, err := reader.Resolve(selector)\n193|\tif err != nil {\n194|\t\treturn Summary{}, err\n195|\t}\n196|\tprojection, err := (&sessstate.Projector{Repo: selected.repo, LocalHostID: reader.LocalHostID}).Project(selected.SessionID)\n197|\tif err != nil {\n198|\t\treturn Summary{}, err\n199|\t}\n200|\tsummary := Summary{Projection: projection}\n201|\tif err := checkSummaryRepresentable(summary); err != nil {\n202|\t\treturn Summary{}, err\n203|\t}\n204|\treturn summary, nil\n205|}\n206|\n207|// InspectLocal reads one local ID, including a parked or tombstoned session.\n208|func (reader *Reader) InspectLocal(sessionID string) (Summary, error) {\n209|\tif reader == nil || reader.Local == nil {\n210|\t\treturn Summary{}, fmt.Errorf(\"%w: local repository is required\", ErrUnavailable)\n211|\t}\n212|\tprojection, err := (&sessstate.Projector{Repo: reader.Local, LocalHostID: reader.LocalHostID}).Project(sessionID)\n213|\tif err != nil {\n214|\t\treturn Summary{}, err\n215|\t}\n216|\treturn Summary{Projection: projection}, nil\n217|}\n218|\n219|// Selection identifies the session and source index, never an attach or mutation\n(more lines below)","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000ca39","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0aa4d-35aa-7773-97f7-293f4760a2d6"},"sequence":887,"recorded_at":1780531400001769,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"a1715be3-1f15-4a95-87f8-c19d8786aea9","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"a1715be3-1f15-4a95-87f8-c19d8786aea9","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"a1715be3-1f15-4a95-87f8-c19d8786aea9"},"call_id":"call_01a0aa4f602d7515879c223c01ecf33b","text":"Read text file `internal/sessrepo/sessrepo.go`.\n1|package sessrepo\n2|\n3|import (\n4|\t\"bytes\"\n5|\t\"errors\"\n6|\t\"fmt\"\n7|\t\"os\"\n8|\t\"path/filepath\"\n9|\t\"sync\"\n10|)\n11|\n12|// uint53Max is the AX safe-integer ceiling from SPEC.md Section 1.6. It is\n13|// passed to the environ bound checker, never re-enforced here.\n14|const uint53Max = uint64(1<<53 - 1)\n15|\n16|const (\n17|\tsessionRecordSchema = \"urn:ax:schema:session-record\"\n18|\tsessionEventSchema  = \"urn:ax:schema:session-event\"\n19|)\n20|\n21|var (\n22|\tErrInvalidRecord   = errors.New(\"invalid session record\")\n23|\tErrSessionExists   = errors.New(\"session already exists\")\n24|\tErrUnknownSession  = errors.New(\"unknown session\")\n25|\tErrInvalidEvent    = errors.New(\"invalid session event\")\n26|\tErrSequenceGap     = errors.New(\"event source sequence gap\")\n27|\tErrSequenceRepeat  = errors.New(\"event source sequence repeat\")\n28|\tErrPredecessorLink = errors.New(\"event predecessor link mismatch\")\n29|\tErrDivergentBranch = errors.New(\"divergent lease branch preserved without application\")\n30|\tErrStaleLease      = errors.New(\"event lease epoch precedes the chain head\")\n31|\tErrChainCorrupt    = errors.New(\"session event chain is corrupt\")\n32|\tErrUnknownEvent    = errors.New(\"unknown session event\")\n33|\tErrNameAmbiguous   = errors.New(\"name_ambiguous\")\n34|\tErrNameNotFound    = errors.New(\"session name not found\")\n35|\tErrRepositoryPath  = errors.New(\"invalid session repository path\")\n36|)\n37|\n38|// refuse is the single refusal funnel every sessrepo rejection flows\n39|// through. It is a var so the census TestMain can wrap it and record the\n40|// production file:line behind each exercised refusal. No production path\n41|// wraps a sentinel with fmt.Errorf directly.\n42|var refuse = func(sentinel error, format string, arguments ...any) error {\n43|\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"%w: %s\", sentinel, fmt.Sprintf(format, arguments...))\n44|}\n45|\n46|// SessionRef names one persisted session: its Session Record digest and ID.\n47|type SessionRef struct {\n48|\tSessionID string\n49|\tRecordID  string\n50|}\n51|\n52|// EventRef names one chained event: its digest, lease sequence, and position.\n53|type EventRef struct {\n54|\tSessionID     string\n55|\tEventID       string\n56|\tLeaseSequence uint64\n57|\tPosition      int\n58|}\n59|\n60|// EventSummary is the chain-index entry for one event, derived from the\n61|// validated event bytes at append time and re-verified against them on load.\n62|type EventSummary struct {\n63|\tEventID       string   `json:\"event_id\"`\n64|\tEventType     string   `json:\"event_type\"`\n65|\tLeaseEpoch    uint64   `json:\"lease_epoch\"`\n66|\tLeaseID       string   `json:\"lease_id\"`\n67|\tLeaseSequence uint64   `json:\"lease_sequence\"`\n68|\tPredecessors  []string `json:\"predecessors\"`\n69|}\n70|\n71|// SessionSummary is the Section 14.4 list projection this leaf owns: stored\n72|// identity plus chain-head facts for a healthy session, or the per-session\n73|// parked channel for an interrupted create or a torn store. Owner host,\n74|// checkpoint age, capability status, and rendered warnings are derived\n75|// downstream, never here; the parked fields below are the facts the\n76|// Section 5.7 reducer and the Section 14.4 rendering leaves project from.\n77|//\n78|// A healthy entry carries Parked=false with empty BlockingReason and\n79|// RetryHint. A parked entry carries Parked=true, SessionID set to the\n80|// session directory name, BlockingReason naming the load failure (a\n81|// recoverable_parked_state block with its per-session cause), and RetryHint\n82|// naming the same-operation retry. Identity members (RecordID, Name, Kind,\n83|// ProviderID) are filled from the parked record when it still verifies;\n84|// a bare directory with no verifiable record leaves them empty.\n85|type SessionSummary struct {\n86|\tSessionID      string\n87|\tRecordID       string\n88|\tName           string\n89|\tKind           string\n90|\tProviderID     string\n91|\tEventCount     int\n92|\tTailEvent      string\n93|\tParked         bool\n94|\tBlockingReason string\n95|\tRetryHint      string\n96|}\n97|\n98|// retryHintForParkedRecord names the same-operation retry for a parked\n99|// session: a record is already parked, so only the byte-identical record\n100|// resumes through CreateSession.\n(more lines below)","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
