{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000ca99","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0aa4d-35aa-7773-97f7-293f4760a2d6"},"sequence":935,"recorded_at":1780531400001865,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"a1715be3-1f15-4a95-87f8-c19d8786aea9","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"a1715be3-1f15-4a95-87f8-c19d8786aea9","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"a1715be3-1f15-4a95-87f8-c19d8786aea9"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0aa4f-f3a2-7ea0-8897-7dafbe77489c"},"task_id":"01a0aa4f-f3a2-7ea0-8897-7dafbe77489c","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0aa4f-f3a2-7ea0-8897-7dafbe77489c","chunk":"{\n  \"chunk_id\": \"exec-18-1\",\n  \"command\": \"grep -n \\\"first launch\\\\|later launch\\\\|launch.*checkpoint\\\\|checkpoint.*launch\\\" internal/specdoc/SPEC.md | head -n 40\",\n  \"description\": \"Search launch-checkpoint linkage in spec\",\n  \"exit_code\": 0,\n  \"terminal_status\": \"completed\",\n  \"output\": \"1809:for the first launch, the Session Record and null. A non-null source MUST name\\n2277:| <code>creating</code> | Session record and initial lease exist; no first validated checkpoint exists and bootstrap launch/retry is in progress |\\n8159:| <code>BOOT-DIRECT-AFTER-TERMINAL</code> | Wrapper exists; no provider process or checkpoint | Resume reuses that wrapper and retries launch once; force stop removes only the inert wrapper after closure proof |\\n8161:| <code>BOOT-DIRECT-AFTER-IDENTITY</code> | Identity/event exist; no checkpoint | Resume validates the same identity and continues capture; it MUST NOT call provider new-session launch |\\n9059:| Epoch-1 launch fails before first checkpoint | Never report stopped/resumable or invent a checkpoint | Reconcile and retry the same bootstrap identity, establish the first checkpoint, or prove closure and record non-resumable bootstrap abort |\\n9108:| <code>CR-LAUNCH-TB-01..03</code> | Task-board bootstrap: after session/lease/event persistence; bridge launch may have returned a manager reference; bridge export may have returned a bundle/proof, each before the next Section 13.2 durable phase or first-checkpoint publication. |\\n11920:| <code>AC-LAUNCH-001</code> | Direct launch creates record/lease/wrapper/provider identity/checkpoint and native resume works outside <code>ax</code>. |\\n11946:| <code>AC-BOOT-001</code> | Every epoch-1 pre-checkpoint direct/task-board launch failure is either idempotently retried under the same process/manager identity, promoted through a first checkpoint, or force-closed as a null-checkpoint non-resumable failed bootstrap; RPC/Event/CLI shapes agree. |\\n12222:| Epoch-1 failed launch had no stop/resume representation | Sections 5.2, 5.7, 11.3, 13.1–13.2, 13.9–13.10, and 14.2 define bootstrap retry/abort, nullable checkpoint, non-resumable failed state, and exact RPC/Event/CLI agreement; <code>AC-BOOT-001</code> covers every boundary |\\n12224:| Effective profile authority conflicted with events/bundles | Sections 2.4, 5.2, 5.4, 9.3, 11.3, and 13 repeat one checkpoint-derived effective profile/source through launch, bundle, takeover, resume, and fork, including Pi's equal mapping; <code>AC-PROFILE-001</code> covers both persistence paths |\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 2246,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 562,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}","final_result":true}}}
