{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000d6df","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0aa4d-35aa-7773-97f7-293f4760a2d6"},"sequence":2506,"recorded_at":1780531400005007,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"a1715be3-1f15-4a95-87f8-c19d8786aea9","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"a1715be3-1f15-4a95-87f8-c19d8786aea9","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"a1715be3-1f15-4a95-87f8-c19d8786aea9"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0aa6d-e760-7e71-ae61-7a5fce93aa54"},"task_id":"01a0aa6d-e760-7e71-ae61-7a5fce93aa54","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0aa6d-e760-7e71-ae61-7a5fce93aa54","chunk":"Read text file `internal/sessquery/TRACEABILITY.md`.\n(149 line(s) above)\n150|  referenced Session Record kind selects: direct sessions admit only\n151|  provider-manifest checkpoints and task_board sessions only\n152|  task-board-bundle checkpoints, and each admitting its Section\n153|  2.4 profile authority over the same closure through\n154|  `checkCheckpointProfileAuthority` (transitive predecessor\n155|  closure from the winning source chain with the Session Record\n156|  creation profile: the first launch carries the creation pair,\n157|  later launches and resumes carry the newest authoritative\n158|  profile.changed event at or before them with its target\n159|  profile; missing, out-of-closure, wrong-type, and non-newest\n160|  sources plus stale values refuse integrity_failure; historical\n161|  heads stay admissible because derivation never consults the\n162|  current tail). The winning triple binds from\n163|  that same record; envelope triples never substitute for it. A\n164|  session with no admitted winning record refuses\n165|  selector_observation_unavailable; a complete read proving no lease\n166|  refuses selector_bootstrap_incomplete instead of binding an empty\n167|  triple. The provhost no-attestation-outside-the-leaf bound now\n168|  allowlists five session-leaf sites (the two entry decodes, the\n169|  load re-verification, and both record attestations).\n170|- `authority_heads` binds the sorted unique validated lease, event,\n171|  and tombstone heads used for the decision: the winning Lease\n172|  Record digest plus the tail event digest of every allowed source\n173|  holding a non-parked copy of the pinned session. The complete\n174|  authority union (same record, current tombstones, greatest winning\n175|  lease across the local and every allowlisted source) is validated\n176|  at build and at every revalidation; a parked copy of the pinned\n177|  session in any required source fails the union closed with\n178|  selector_observation_unavailable instead of contributing a head;\n179|  unrelated index changes stay conservative stale.\n180|- `source_host_id` is always a bound UUIDv7: a local selection\n181|  without a known local host refuses invalid_config at build time.\n182|- Wire exit binding (CLI Result 5 with Structured Error 1.4.0) belongs\n183|  to its owning leaf; this library keeps refusal classes distinct and\n184|  stable under their normative spellings without registering codes.\n185|- Record-only chains keep the accepted internal projection with empty\n186|  owner/lease facts inside the projector. The list/status summary\n187|  entries refuse them, while explicit local inspection retains raw\n188|  access to the recovery diagnostics. The 14.7.4 recovery flow itself\n189|  belongs to the bootstrap leaf with the accepted projector behavior\n190|  reconciled in its scoped review; this leaf invents neither a state\n191|  nor an error for it.\n192|- Effect authorization (fencing, commit, retry, recovery, remote\n193|  dispatch/admission, transport-resume) and the composed\n194|  invocation-to-plan bindings for attach and logs belong to the CLI\n195|  and lifecycle owners, which invoke `Revalidate` at every boundary in\n196|  `BoundariesFor`. Plans built here authorize read projection only.\n197|- Reads across multiple `Projector.Project` calls are not an atomic\n198|  repository/mesh snapshot; concurrent writers, fresh peer\n199|  acquisition, cross-peer lease union, and differing replicated views\n200|  are not measured. Transports, peer authentication, freshness, mesh\n201|  union, host metadata, and observation contracts remain upstream\n202|  boundaries: configuration, learned indexes, host metadata, and\n203|  observations arrive as trusted caller inputs, and the allowlist proof\n204|  covers filtering, never attestation. The repository/projector own\n205|  record/event admission and validation. No new external provider,\n206|  filesystem durability, terminal, RPC, or CLI capability is attested.","final_result":true}}}
