e whole\\n1198:literal — `epoch != 1` — was proven only at epoch 4: narrowing it to\\n1201:`epoch > 1` is an equivalent mutant, so no deletion or operator sweep could ever\\n1225:An audit sweep generates its mutants from that same derivation rather than from\\n1228:external harness can only mutate what the gates themselves derive. Forty mutants\\n1232:non-negative domain whose minimum is `K` it is an equivalent mutant, and\\n1233:reporting an equivalent mutant as a kill is how an earlier sweep on this leaf\\n1285:narrowing one clause cannot pass on a neighbouring clause's refusal.\\n1329:widening mutant at the source; it does not establish that a JSON path in a real\\n1332:unchanged and admit `stop` on a lease, and that mutant is refused here. Each\\n1367:Five mutants — a lease vocabulary widened with another record's value, a\\n1372:existing coupling inventory, which owns that clause. A seventh mutant, skipping\\n1374:tests and the whole package suite: it is an equivalent mutant, because every\\n1391:against one language-neutral SHA-256 identity. Validation uses fixed `100x`\\n1452:SHA-256, performs an OS-native atomic no-replace rename, then fsyncs the shard\\n1679:vector and a length-only narrowing mutant.\\n1715:survivors; 16 narrowing, 10 arm-deletion, 4 census-only, 3 audit-only; plus\\n===\\n51:  profile-only substitution. New narrowing plants\\n55:  SURVIVED control; full 59-plant battery re-run green on final\\n79:  narrowing mutant Revalidate/BuildPlan return nil (strong kill),\\n132:- FINDING 4 (narrowing): all seven `&& false` clause-disables replaced\\n135:  triple+attestation, two-event chain), plus new narrowings for both\\n166:  empty; narrowing battery re-derived on the final tree (29 KILLED, 0\\n175:- EVIDENCE: all 26 configured local gates passed; later focused config rework passed and the final handoff reruns the same gates on its captured candidate. Eleven narrowing mutants each produced semantic assertion failures with 11 passing instrumentation controls; token-preserving stale generator directive still passes the static token check and fails the behavioral CLI suite. Mutations ran in a task-scoped copy and were restored byte-exact. One initial M4 applicator failed because instrumentation split its exact needle; that attempt is recorded as setup failure, not a kill, and the corrected battery re-proved all rows. Archived per-command exits supersede the prior unarchived battery claims.\\n176:- FIGURES: contracts=63, normative section keys=36, acceptance cases=101, fixtures=32, historical contracts=55; bindings=56 (full=1, partial=3, sliver=1, unevidenced=48, unmeasured=3), unowned=12, discharged clauses=17/463. README's stale 53/428 sample was corrected. The 17 existing discharges are preserved; no new runtime clause is claimed.\\n180:- PROVENANCE (verified this session, upstream read-only): `verify-tag v0.6.0` exit 0 (tag object `40c123eb…861a785`, ECDSA `SHA256:V6JiKG7J29mjsvikcLoSVp0bLa77VTsFy12gnLO81cM`), peeled commit `0cbdf100…67859a6` (`verify-commit` exit 0, `ls-remote` peeled ref equal), SPEC.md 1150005 bytes SHA256 `74504539…90896b` measured from the tagged blob. Delivery is the signed git tag; no hosted GitHub Release exists (release-verdict archive), so only immutable commit/blob URLs are referenced.\\n184:- MUTANTS (4 narrowing, each admits exactly one member, each kills exactly its named subtest, full suites otherwise green, all restored cmp-clean): M1 digest+trailing-newline, M2 identity+stale-commit (v0.6.0 tokens preserved), M3 ParseV060+stale-v0.5.0-doc, M4 token-preserving delta-row Versions drop. Detail in `.temp/TASK-260908-3kvnm2/mutant-results.md`.\\n207:- EVIDENCE: outcome `TASK-260830-1r9wrr_outcome.md` rev2 (10/10 AC rows unchanged, gate table, censuses, 28/28 killed battery over 14 narrowing incl. N13/N14 on the union/local derivation + 8 arm-deletion + 3 census-test + 3 audit-only, XN the single intended survivor with its bound, tree OID + exact 16 paths). Harness `.temp/TASK-260830-1r9wrr/mutate.sh` (gitignored scratch), rev2 log attached.\\n215:- EVIDENCE: outcome `TASK-260830-1r9wrr_outcome.md` on the board task (10/10 AC rows with call sites, gate table, three censuses, 26/26 killed battery with narrowing/arm-deletion/census-test/audit-only + NOT_APPLIED/COMPILE_FAIL rows, tree OID + exact changed paths). Harness `.temp/TASK-260830-1r9wrr/mutate.sh` (gitignored scratch), log attached.\\n222:- NUMBERS (re-derived, not re-typed): refusal census 35 = chain.go 25 + sessrepo.go 5 + store.go 5 (README's 36 fixed in place); equality census 2 sites = 2 ledger rows; battery 33 applied / 33 killed / 0 survivors (16 narrowing N1–N16, 10 arm-deletion D1–D10, 4 census-only C1–C4 incl. both reviewer plant shapes, 3 audit-only A1–A3) + NOT_APPLIED/COMPILE_FAIL controls distinct. Candidate tree by detached-index `write-tree`; outcome enumerates exactly the 11 CR paths. Also fixed the N2 comment wording (`sessrepo_test.go`): the canonical owner refuses one arm later, not earlier (member arms run before Verify).\\n228:- F1 CORRECTION (supersedes the round-1 entry below): \\\"schema gate precedes every Verify call\\\" was false — `loadSessionLocked` re-verifies stored blobs through Verify with no schema gate, and the verbatim SPEC §5.5 provider-identity record verifies cleanly there (recomputed digest matches; only `field != SelfEventID` refuses). Restated everywhere the false universal stood (`identity.go` comment, `identity_test.go` bound, `sessrepo/doc.go` authority split, README, outcome): entry decodes gate schema before Verify; the load path recomputes whatever digest stored bytes claim and refuses non-`event_id` self fields / index-disagreeing digests at named arms. Gating the load path instead would have made the field arm unreachable-by-construction (Verify resolves the self field from the same schema member) and its narrowing mutant unkillable — measured, not assumed. The load verify is now three single-line refuse rows (verify failure, self field, digest), each with its own boundary plant; the shared message that formatted a nil error is gone.\\n230:- F2 BATTERY: 26 applied / 26 killed / 0 survivors (12 narrowing, 10 arm-deletion, 2 census-only, 2 audit-only; NOT_APPLIED + COMPILE_FAIL distinct), denominator extended to load/recovery: provider-identity plant kills the field narrowing (M1a), blob-swap kills the digest narrowing (M1b), exclusive-create-first blob install kills O_EXCL→O_TRUNC (M2, witnessed through a fresh handle sharing no mutex/memory), same-length collision kills the resume-equality narrowing (M6), cross-session record kills the session-half drop (M7), rebound-predecessor detached index kills the digest-half drop behaviorally (M8 — the old detached test passes via the continuity arm and is kept as the precision control). Measured bound: the verify-error arm is behaviorally subsumed by the field arm (Verify returns field \\\"\\\" on every error path) — diagnostic attribution + census row, no deletion mutant, stated in the outcome. Harness at `.temp/TASK-260830-wbpf1v/mutation_battery.sh` (gitignored scratch) with exact-count application and checksum restore; log attached to the board task.\\n240:- EVIDENCE: outcome `TASK-260830-wbpf1v_outcome.md` on the board task (10/10 AC rows with call sites, gate table, census + 12/12 killed mutation battery with narrowing/arm-deletion/census-only/audit-only + NOT_APPLIED/COMPILE_FAIL rows, tree OID + exact changed paths recorded there). Battery harness at `/tmp/mutation_battery.sh` (throwaway, not committed).\\n249:- R4: new `TestSameBlockSentencesSplitOnTerminal` (period/bang/query rows, same-block negated+positive pair) kills the paragraph-granularity narrowing (N-split-X1) and the dot-only narrowing (N-split-dot-only).\\n254:- EVIDENCE: outcome `TASK-260907-9ny4xl_outcome.md` (5/5 AC rows with call sites, battery table, tree OID, exact changed paths) + `TASK-260907-9ny4xl_mutants.log` + `TASK-260907-9ny4xl_change-request.patch` on the board task. Battery 14 applied / 14 killed / 0 survivors (narrowing 10 incl. the token-preserving directive rewrite, arm-deletion 3, census-only 1; C-old-corpus census control; NOT_APPLIED/COMPILE_FAIL distinct harness rows; audit-only 0 — no AST audit in this CR's scope).\\n261:- F2 (duplicate class measured at one key): narrowing `duplicate && key != K` survived 6/8 response keys and 7/10 owner keys. Fix: derivation-backed sweepers (member sets derived from tuple/observation/response/scan-request production; new members auto-swept) through `DecodeTuple`/`CheckScanRequest`/`DecodeManifest`/`DecodeResponse`/`DecodeStrictObject`. Battery adds 8 owner + 6 retained narrowing mutants, one per survived key. Survivor honest-report: first `P_dupnarrow_provider_id` run SURVIVED and exposed a real test gap (foreign `provider_id` missing from the envelope sweeper); key added, mutant re-run KILLED.\\n262:- F3 (denominator basis): corrected — 31 refuse sites + 59 bool-false + 11 `&Fault{}` frame exits = 101 (105 counting the 4 bool-`return <expr>` arms: CheckEnvironmentID/CheckSemver/isNull/rawUint53-forward). The \\\"27 of 100\\\" figure was the corrected basis pre-ladder-guard; 90 was the uncorrected one. Harness derives all three components at runtime; F3 residue exits attacked by N1/M15/M15n/M16/M17/M17n inside the previously excluded 11.\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 10352,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 2588,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"bash","outcome":"success"}}}
