{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000d719","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0aa4d-35aa-7773-97f7-293f4760a2d6"},"sequence":2535,"recorded_at":1780531400005065,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"a1715be3-1f15-4a95-87f8-c19d8786aea9","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"a1715be3-1f15-4a95-87f8-c19d8786aea9","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"a1715be3-1f15-4a95-87f8-c19d8786aea9"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0aa6e-09cf-7102-9d81-20b2ea281711"},"task_id":"01a0aa6e-09cf-7102-9d81-20b2ea281711","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0aa6e-09cf-7102-9d81-20b2ea281711","chunk":"Read text file `LOGBOOK.md`.\n1|# Flight Logbook\n2|\n3|> Institutional memory. Concise, factual, high-signal.\n4|> Newest entries first. One block per insight.\n5|\n6|## 2026-09-10\n7|\n8|### TASK-260830-21gygk — rev8 rework: checkpoint profile authority admitted over the event-head closure\n9|- DEFECT (repeat of the canonical-identity family, C6 relationship):\n10|  `checkCheckpointEventHeads` resolved digests/tuples without profile\n11|  payloads, so a first launch citing a dangling all-zero source kept\n12|  every head/session/lease/creator/persistence check green and was\n13|  admitted by all four shared entries (CR8 P1, reviewer\n14|  `TestRev8CheckpointProfileAuthority` red baseline recorded pre-fix\n15|  in `.temp/TASK-260830-21gygk/rev8-baseline-red.log`: 4 controls\n16|  passed, 4 missing-source negatives admitted).\n17|- FIX (shared admission path, `internal/sessquery/lease.go`): new\n18|  `checkCheckpointProfileAuthority` runs after the heads gate for the\n19|  winner and every necessary ancestor at all four entries. It walks\n20|  the transitive predecessor closure from the winning-source chain\n21|  (`ListEvents` predecessors; genesis link must name the Session\n22|  Record, anything else dangling is integrity_failure; divergent\n23|  blobs outside the index never enter), reads the creation profile\n24|  via `GetRecord`, and binds every launch/resume pair in chain\n25|  order: first launch carries (creation, null), later pairs carry\n26|  the newest authoritative profile.changed at or before them with\n27|  its target; missing/out-of-closure/wrong-type/non-newest sources\n28|  and stale values refuse integrity_failure per SPEC 5.4. Only the\n29|  change target feeds derivation (source/confirmation belong to\n30|  publication); fork.created keeps its shape-pinned null source plus\n31|  cross-session provenance and is not re-derived here. Losing-lease\n32|  changes are observable as preserved-but-unindexed blobs (sessrepo\n33|  `AppendEvent` divergent arm) and refuse as unknown sources; a\n34|  well-formed future citation from inside the closure has no fixture\n35|  by causal necessity (continuity forces every prior event into the\n36|  closure), and the historical control proves later events are never\n37|  consulted instead.\n38|- MUTANT INTERACTION (recorded, not hidden): the new closure backstop\n39|  also refuses the all-zero head, so `N-checkpoint-heads` briefly\n40|  SURVIVED (weakened heads still green via profile refusal).\n41|  `TestRev7CheckpointHeadAuthority` now pins the\n42|  observation_unavailable class for missing/later heads\n43|  (`rev7CheckHeadRefusalClass` + old-plan pin): unmutated heads fire\n44|  first, the weakened-heads plant is KILLED again by wrong-class\n45|  instead of silent admission, and gate order is locked.\n46|- TESTS: ported reviewer probe kept as `TestRev8CheckpointProfileAuthority`;\n47|  new `rev8_regression_test.go` adds real-change positives\n48|  (launch/resume/two-generation, direct/task_board winner+ancestor,\n49|  fresh-plan revalidation), eight refusal classes with the integrity\n50|  class pinned, historical-closure admission, and old-plan\n51|  profile-only substitution. New narrowing plants\n52|  `N-profile-first-source`, `N-profile-newest`, `N-profile-value`,\n53|  and token-preserving `N-profile-change-direction` (from-for-to)\n54|  are KILLED through the same instrument with the applied harmless\n55|  SURVIVED control; full 59-plant battery re-run green on final\n56|  source (only the three design controls report separately).\n57|- DOCS: TRACEABILITY SelectionPlan row + six new refusal rows state\n58|  the gate, call sites, tests, and plants. Work left uncommitted in\n59|  the Story worktree for board CR.\n60|\n61|### TASK-260830-21gygk rev4 rework: winning-lease succession, parked fail-closed, closed capability vocabulary\n62|- CHAIN+CHECKPOINT (`internal/sessquery/lease.go`): `winningLeaseFor`\n63|  now validates the full succession after greatest-tuple selection.\n64|  `checkLeaseChain` walks the admitted ancestry by epoch plus one to\n65|  an epoch-1 null root; self/cycle/skip/contradictory/duplicate links\n66|  are `integrity_failure`, missing names/records stay\n67|  `selector_observation_unavailable`. `checkWinnerCheckpoint`\n68|  resolves the winner's `checkpoint_id` against admitted\n69|  `Reader.CheckpointRecords` (new input, new\n70|  `sessrepo.AttestCheckpointRecord` owner; provhost\n71|  no-attestation-outside-the-leaf bound 4→5 with justification):\n72|  successors must name a validated record for their session bound to\n73|  the predecessor lease, epoch-1 roots may carry none or a\n74|  self-bound one. Unresolvable references are\n75|  observation_unavailable, never absence.\n76|- PARKED (`revalidate.go`): `checkUnionCopy` fails a parked pinned\n77|  copy closed with observation_unavailable at build and revalidate.\n78|  The agreeing-record fixture isolates this gate: under the\n79|  narrowing mutant Revalidate/BuildPlan return nil (strong kill),\n80|  while the divergent member shifts to record-agreement integrity\n(more lines below)","final_result":true}}}
