{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000d7d9","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0aa4d-35aa-7773-97f7-293f4760a2d6"},"sequence":2631,"recorded_at":1780531400005257,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"a1715be3-1f15-4a95-87f8-c19d8786aea9","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"a1715be3-1f15-4a95-87f8-c19d8786aea9","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"a1715be3-1f15-4a95-87f8-c19d8786aea9"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0aa6e-8999-7490-a967-2356edfdb762"},"task_id":"01a0aa6e-8999-7490-a967-2356edfdb762","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0aa6e-8999-7490-a967-2356edfdb762","chunk":"Read text file `README.md`.\n(1832 line(s) above)\n1833|## Session selector, read summaries, and selection plans\n1834|\n1835|`internal/sessquery` is the single shared selector API over the persisted\n1836|session repositories and the accepted state projector. It implements the\n1837|v0.6.0 selector contract (§14.7/§14.7.1, refining §2.3) with shared\n1838|SelectionPlan construction and revalidation (§14.7.2):\n1839|\n1840|- Literal grammar: split at the first `@` only. The key is a NAME, a bare\n1841|  UUID (name-first precedence kept), or `id:UUID` (bypasses names for the\n1842|  durable union identity). The source is empty (bare §2.3 tiers), `local`,\n1843|  `peer:ALIAS` (the entire remaining suffix, literal — spaces, `@`,\n1844|  Unicode, and `%` included), or `id:HOST_UUID`. No joining, aliasing,\n1845|  percent-decoding, Unicode normalization, trimming, or alias folding.\n1846|- Exact source mappings: effective configuration (local host, peer\n1847|  alias/host mappings, allowlist) is validated first, including exact\n1848|  alias and host-ID uniqueness; duplicates are `invalid_config`.\n1849|  Explicit unknown aliases/hosts are `selector_source_not_found`; known\n1850|  but disallowed peers are `peer_not_allowlisted`. Remote read failures\n1851|  are `selector_source_read_failed` with the cause preserved; local I/O\n1852|  keeps its repository error; malformed authority is `integrity_failure`.\n1853|- No explicit-source fallback: a qualified key resolves in its one\n1854|  source only. Tier, collision, and tombstone semantics follow §14.7.1:\n1855|  exact live name then UUID-shaped name within the source, replicated\n1856|  copies deduplicate only on agreeing record digests (else\n1857|  `integrity_failure`), distinct colliding names refuse with\n1858|  `name_ambiguous`, and tombstoned entries stay excluded on\n1859|  authoritative tombstone evidence while failed reads never count as it.\n1860|- Immutable plans: `Reader.BuildPlan` binds all sixteen §14.7.2\n1861|  members — the literal selector, session and validated record digest,\n1862|  source host (always a UUIDv7; a local selection without a known local\n1863|  host refuses `invalid_config`) and exact alias, index and\n1864|  configuration digests, the validated winning `urn:ax:schema:lease`\n1865|  Lease Record digest with its epoch, lease ID, and holder from that\n1866|  same record (admitted through the canonicaljson owner from\n1867|  `Reader.LeaseRecords`, greatest (epoch, lease_id) winner with a\n1868|  fully validated succession: the predecessor ancestry chains by\n1869|  epoch plus one to an epoch-1 null-predecessor root, and every\n1870|  lease in that winning ancestry above epoch 1 references an\n1871|  admitted `urn:ax:schema:checkpoint` Checkpoint Record from\n1872|  `Reader.CheckpointRecords` for its session and predecessor lease,\n1873|  each created by the owning lease holder, each carrying the\n1874|  persistence variant the referenced Session Record kind selects\n1875|  (direct only provider-manifest, task_board only task-board-bundle;\n1876|  §5.4), and each resolving every event head to a chained event for\n1877|  its session at or before its bound lease in the winning source\n1878|  chain (historical heads admissible, never required to equal the\n1879|  current tail; missing, cross-session, losing-lease, and later-lease\n1880|  heads refuse); no envelope\n1881|  observation substitutes for it),\n1882|  lease/event/tombstone authority heads (winning lease digest plus\n1883|  every non-parked source tail, sorted unique), action, destination,\n1884|  and expectation digest. A session with no admitted winning record\n1885|  refuses `selector_observation_unavailable`; a complete read proving\n1886|  a record without any valid lease refuses\n1887|  `selector_bootstrap_incomplete` instead of binding an empty triple.\n1888|  `Reader.Revalidate` compares every bound fact in a fixed order and\n1889|  validates the complete authority union for the pinned UUID across\n1890|  the local and every allowlisted source — contradictory records are\n1891|  `integrity_failure`, a greater winning lease and fresh tombstone\n1892|  evidence are `selector_plan_stale` while lagging copies stay\n1893|  current, and a parked copy of the pinned session in any required\n1894|  source fails the union closed with\n1895|  `selector_observation_unavailable` (never evidence, never absence)\n1896|  — without re-resolving names or substituting selections.\n1897|  Revocation is `peer_not_allowlisted`, and reads keep their classes.\n1898|  Plans authorize read projection only; fencing, commit, and remote\n1899|  routes belong to the CLI/lifecycle callers that invoke revalidation.\n1900|\n1901|`Reader.List` and `Reader.Status` read actual Session Records and event\n1902|chains through `sessrepo` and `sessstate.Projector`. They expose the\n1903|derived identity, provider, lifecycle, winning lease/owner, local role,\n1904|checkpoint ID, conflicts, and warnings as an internal `Summary`. List\n1905|order is bytewise session ID; `InspectLocal` retains raw access to\n1906|parked/tombstoned IDs and recovery diagnostics and is not a public\n1907|summary entry. Failed index reads and failed projections propagate as\n1908|errors. Repository-parked sessions remain visible in listing but are\n1909|excluded from live routing. Reading never repairs a store or performs\n1910|an attach, resume, or ownership change. Creating is a record AND an\n1911|authoritative initial lease (§5.7/§13.1 step 2), so a record-only chain\n1912|is an interrupted prefix for the bootstrap-recovery leaf: list and\n1913|status refuse it with `selector_bootstrap_incomplete` — the whole list\n1914|when any encountered record is unrepresentable — instead of returning\n1915|an ownerless row or a placeholder owner. The closed authoritative\n1916|layer (`Reader.AuthoritativeStatus`, `Reader.AuthoritativeList`)\n1917|binds owner, lease, and role from the validated winning Lease Record,\n1918|owner display names only from validated host metadata (1..64), local\n1919|roles only with a known local host, checkpoint timestamps only from\n1920|validated observations, workspace_status from the closed five-value\n1921|enum, capabilities from validated CapabilitySummary maps (0..7, only\n1922|available may enable) keyed by exactly the provhost-owned Section 7.3\n1923|seven-name provider registry (any other name refuses\n1924|`invalid_config`), process liveness as a required boolean for\n1925|status, and warnings from the projection; unknown required\n1926|observations refuse `selector_observation_unavailable` while\n1927|established absence (workspace absent, empty non-nil capabilities)\n1928|stays representable, and nothing is inferred.\n1929|\n1930|These entries do not provide an `ax` executable or a closed CLI Result\n1931|renderer. CLI Result 5 with Structured Error 1.4.0, wire exit binding,\n1932|transports, peer authentication, and lifecycle effects belong to their\n1933|owning leaves.\n1934|`TestCreatingSummaryCannotClaimClosedCLIResult` drives the refused\n1935|`Reader.List`/`Reader.Status` entries and the existing `cliresult.New`\n1936|to demonstrate that a creating session without owner facts satisfies\n1937|neither the summary entries nor the mandatory CLI owner/lease fields.\n1938|No owner is invented and no doctor/provider/platform capability\n1939|is advertised. The traceability, gate battery, and remaining bounds are\n1940|in [the task evidence map](internal/sessquery/TRACEABILITY.md).\n1941|\n1942|```bash\n1943|go test ./internal/sessquery ./internal/sessrepo -count=1 -v\n1944|python3 internal/sessquery/testdata/mutate.py /absolute/path/to/new/evidence-dir\n1945|```\n1946|\n1947|## Structured Errors, Stable Codes, and Causal Redaction\n1948|\n1949|[`internal/axerror`](internal/axerror) implements the Section 15 Structured\n1950|Error contract: the closed versioned failure object, its stable code-to-exit\n1951|registry, its retryability rule, its typed diagnostic details, and the redaction\n1952|that keeps a local cause off the wire. The package holds no state, opens no\n(more lines below)","final_result":true}}}
