backstop), and each admitting its Section 2.4 profile authority over the same closure (first launch carries the creation pair, later launches and resumes carry the newest authoritative change with its target profile; missing, losing, and non-newest sources plus stale values refuse integrity_failure while later local-only changes are never consulted); narrowing mutants `N-ancestor-checkpoint`, `N-checkpoint-holder`, `N-ancestor-holder`, `N-checkpoint-persistence`, `N-checkpoint-heads`, `N-profile-first-source`, `N-profile-newest`, `N-profile-value`, and `N-profile-change-direction` admit exactly one member of each guarded class), fixed compare order with per-member stale reasons, revocation class, cross-source integrity class, read/projection failure classes, tamper-evident persistence where digest equality never substitutes for revalidation. The union winner is the greatest tuple across all allowed sources (lagging copies stay current, greater copies are stale); a parked copy of the pinned session in any required source fails the union closed with selector_observation_unavailable (never evidence, never absence); authority heads bind the winning lease digest plus every non-parked source tail, sorted unique. A same-name gain for another UUID never retargets the pinned plan; an agreeing replica never invalidates it. |\\n100:| Profile first-launch pair | `TestRev8CheckpointProfileAuthority` (missing_source on direct/task_board winner and ancestor paths), `TestRev8ProfileSourceRefusals/first_wrong_profile`, `/dangling_resume_source` | N-profile-first-source admits exactly the all-zero source where the creation pair wants null; every other unexpected or missing source still refuses integrity_failure. |\\n101:| Profile newest source | `TestRev8ProfileSourceRefusals/wrong_type` (non-change event), `/non_newest` (superseded change), `/cross_session` (foreign change), `/losing_branch` (preserved divergent-blob change outside the index), `/dangling_resume_source` | N-profile-newest keeps the first change as authority instead of the newest; citations of a superseded source then admit while other source classes still refuse. |\\n115:prove no behavioral kill. Measured runs and per-mutant tables are\\n157:  later launches and resumes carry the newest authoritative\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 7150,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 1788,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}","final_result":true}}}
