{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000d83d","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0aa4d-35aa-7773-97f7-293f4760a2d6"},"sequence":2681,"recorded_at":1780531400005357,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"a1715be3-1f15-4a95-87f8-c19d8786aea9","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"a1715be3-1f15-4a95-87f8-c19d8786aea9","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"a1715be3-1f15-4a95-87f8-c19d8786aea9"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0aa6f-5210-7262-a0b0-90e7f7135902"},"task_id":"01a0aa6f-5210-7262-a0b0-90e7f7135902","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0aa6f-5210-7262-a0b0-90e7f7135902","chunk":"Read text file `internal/sessquery/TRACEABILITY.md`.\n(101 line(s) above)\n102|| Profile effective value | `TestRev8ProfileSourceRefusals/stale_value` (creation fallback past a change), `TestRev8ProfileChangedPositiveControl`, `TestRev8ProfileResumePositiveControl`, `TestRev8ProfileTwoGenerationControl` | N-profile-value admits exactly a yolo-valued pair past the effective-profile compare; every other stale value still refuses integrity_failure. |\n103|| Profile change-target derivation | Same positive controls plus `TestRev8ProfileHistoricalClosureAdmits` | N-profile-change-direction still matches profile.changed and still reads `to` but derives from `from`; the P1/E1 positives fail. The discriminator token is preserved while the authority behavior changes. |\n104|| Historical closure fixation | `TestRev8ProfileHistoricalClosureAdmits` (post-head change never consulted), `TestRev8ProfileOldPlanSubstitution` (old plan refuses a substituted checkpoint whose valid heads cover a stale pair) | Admission behavior with paired refusal coverage above; no separate refusal predicate to narrow. |\n105|| Union parked authority | `TestRevalidateUnionParkedCopyRefuses` (divergent and agreeing arms), `TestRev4ParkedAuthorityMustRefuse` | N-parked-union-refusal admits parked union copies with a nonempty record: the agreeing-record member validates over unknown authority (Revalidate and BuildPlan return nil, the strong kill) while the divergent-record member shifts to the record-agreement refusal. The divergent reviewer probe still refuses through record agreement (documented subsumption). |\n106|| Summary capability vocabulary | `TestRev4UnknownCapabilityMustRefuse`, `TestAuthoritativeAdmitsFullCapabilityRegistry`, `TestAuthoritativeInputValidation/unknown_capability_name` | N-capability-name admits exactly the invented_capability name past the closed registry; every registry name stays admitted and every other invented name still refuses invalid_config. |\n107|| Deterministic order | Order tests above | B-peer-order, B-session-order reverse list orders; B-tie-break reverses the copy tie break. |\n108|\n109|The shipped mutation runner executes the behavioral suites in an\n110|isolated source copy, checks exact replacement count, preserves raw\n111|process exits and named failed tests, then restores and verifies the\n112|copied bytes. It has before/after green controls, a harmless\n113|comment control that must survive through the same instrument, a\n114|not-applied control, and a compile-failure control. The latter two\n115|prove no behavioral kill. Measured runs and per-mutant tables are\n116|attached on the task, never hard-coded as a green claim here. No\n117|new source-text gate lacks its token-preserving mutant: the `@`,\n118|`local`, `id:`, and alias-equality tokens each carry one, the\n119|capability-vocabulary gate carries the invented-name admission plus\n120|the full seven-name positive that preserves every searched-for\n121|token through the behavioral suite, and the profile discriminator\n122|carries the from-for-to derivation mutant that preserves the\n123|`profile.changed` match and the `to` read while changing which\n124|member supplies authority.\n125|\n126|The read and revalidation entries perform no durable writes. The crash\n127|test interrupts the real repository create after record installation,\n128|inspects the parked projection, retries the byte-identical create\n129|through its owner, and observes the healed read. Repeated lists and\n130|revalidations return identical values. This establishes read\n131|idempotency and composition with existing recovery, not a new crash\n(more lines below)","final_result":true}}}
